NAME
       nl - print a file with line numbers

SYNOPSIS
       nl [-b a|t|n] [-w WIDTH] [-s SEPARATOR] [-n ln|rn|rz] [-v START] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       nl copies its input to the output with a number in front of each line.
       By default only lines that are not empty are numbered (-b t). cat -n
       numbers every line.

OPTIONS
       -b, --body-numbering STYLE
              Which lines to number: a all, t non-empty (default), n none.

       -w, --number-width N
              Width of the number column (default 6).

       -s, --number-separator TEXT
              What goes between the number and the line (default a tab).

       -n FORMAT
              ln left-aligned, rn right-aligned (default), rz with zeros.

       -v N   Start counting at N.

EXAMPLES
           nl /etc/fstab
           nl -b a -w 3 -s ': ' script.sh

SEE ALSO
       cat(1), wc(1)
